 "stimulus_html": "<p>“TO THE WOMEN OF THE REPUBLIC:</p>\n<p>We ask you to sign and circulate this petition for the ENTIRE ABOLITION OF SLAVERY. We have now ONE HUNDRED THOUSAND signatures, but we want a MILLION before Congress adjourns. Remember the President’s Proclamation reaches only the Slaves of Rebels. The jails of LOYAL Kentucky are to-day ‘crammed’ with Georgia, Mississippi and Alabama slaves, advertised to be sold for their jail fees ‘According to LAW,’ precisely as before the war!!! While slavery exists ANYWHERE there can be freedom NOWHERE. THERE MUST BE A LAW ABOLISHING SLAVERY. We have undertaken to canvass the Nation for freedom. Women, you cannot vote or fight for your country. Your only way to be a power in the Government is through the exercise of this one, sacred, Constitutional ‘RIGHT OF PETITION;’ and we ask you to use it now to the utmost. Go to the rich, the poor, the high, the low, the soldier, the civilian, the white, the black gather up the names of all who hate slavery all who love LIBERTY, and would have it the LAW of the land and lay them at the feet of Congress, your silent but potent vote for human freedom guarded by the law. . . .</p>\n<p>E. CADY STANTON</p>\n<p>President.</p>\n<p>SUSAN B. ANTHONY,</p>\n<p>Secretary W.L.N. League”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Women’s Loyal National League, “To the Women of the Republic,” January 25, 1864</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
